# Security guardrails

Treat these as **merge blockers** regardless of stack:

| Area | Requirement |
| -------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Authorization** | Every entrypoint validates actor + scope + resource before side effects |
| **Multi-tenant isolation** | Scope column on every tenant row; every query filters; cache/storage key prefixes |
| **Secrets** | Never in source, tests, examples, logs, or chat; inject at deploy |
| **PII** | Classify fields; redact in logs/traces/errors by tier |
| **Input** | Schema validation on all external input; explicit length/range/enum bounds |
| **Queries** | No string interpolation of untrusted input into SQL/NoSQL paths |
| **Dependencies** | Audit critical/high CVEs on a fixed SLA |

## Data classification (four tiers)

| Tier | Examples | Handling |
| ------------ | ---------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |
| Confidential | Passwords, tokens, PAN, API keys | Never store/log plaintext |
| Restricted | Email, phone, government ID | Encrypt sensitive columns; mask in logs |
| Internal | IDs, slugs, correlation IDs | Plain storage; log-safe |
| Public | Names, addresses in public catalog | Plain; log-safe |

